caption: Benefit Value
technology-rule: benefit-value

Benefit Value, or BV, measures how rewarding and useful the chem’s positive effect is.

Calculate BV like DPL, except that limitations representing harm to the user do not reduce Benefit Value.

The following normally reduce both DPL and BV:

Reduced Duration

Accessibility restrictions

Situational limitations

Unreliable effects

Limited scope

Restrictions on what the benefit can accomplish

The following normally reduce DPL but not BV:

Backlash

Temporary Disadvantages

Pain

Nausea

Post-use attribute penalties

Crashes

Harmful withdrawal-like effects

Enhancements such as Extended Duration increase both values.

The GM decides how to classify unusual modifiers.
